      "message": "I am a little reluctant to keep such an out-of-tree patch. We already have facilities to control the version string (the build number is embedded via that mechanism). I do not see the functional issue that is solved with this patch. Does the kernel need to produce said sha anywhere? Also, the kernel/common SHA1 is not really representative for what all goes into a kernel build. Tools and other ingredients are not accounted for in the SHA. Yet, the build number that is usually appended points to a valid manifest to trace back the individual commits of all repositories.",
